{"seq":18,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T03:56:57.653Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0922ddc64688b90dd69fb679fceec9bc233635c61404205d78d21ae3548cf9b2","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through every Moss note I could see (the six public digests under the North and Central team folders). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift went through fine. There's a follow-up note to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nThe two QFL mentions in the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23/26 renewal check-in don't include any ticket numbers. FR-882, #4409 and #4412 show up in the Central digests, but they're Marrow tickets, not QFL. The cheat sheet also warns not to confuse QFL with Quarendon Freightways, which isn't a customer. I only checked Moss's public notes, so there may be other QFL tickets in places I didn't look."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T03:57:01.874Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"03408048a1dda11bbef62fea359bdb985a1a8a22bef258ec1702bad783aebb43","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"I've sent Dana the list in their DM. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers across Moss's six public notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (2025-10-05). Drivers at the Eau Claire yard's gatehouse kiosk weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct 2025, and the customer confirmed the fix the next day.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\", which has no date. The gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14, and the ticket was escalated to tier-2 support.\n\nThe other two notes that mention QFL contain no ticket numbers. The Central team notes do list FR-882, #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Marrow accounts, so I left them out.\n\nI told Dana I only checked Moss's public notes, so there may be other QFL tickets elsewhere. I didn't look through the QFL incident channel, the North team channel or any account ticket files."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
